 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Regular",
   "texto": [
    "**-en** is removed from the infinitive and **-te** is added: **lernen → lernte** (studied), **machen → machte** (did), **arbeiten → arbeitete** (worked).",
    "In plural is added **-ten**: **arbeiteten** (we worked, worked). If the verb ends in **-t** or **-d**, there is a **e** link: **arbeitete**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Unregular",
   "texto": [
    "Some verbs change the vocal and do not carry **-te**: **gehen → ging**, **kommen → kam**, **sehen → sah**, **fahren → fuhr**, **essen → aß**, **trinken → trank**, **schreiben → schrieb**, **lesen → las**.",
    "**Fahren** usually indicates displacement in a vehicle; **gehen** means going or walking, depending on the context. The Präteritum has personal terminations: **ich ging, du gingst, er ging, wir gingen, ihr gingt, sie gingen**."
   ]
  },
